---
# The remote dashboard. It lists ONLY what runs on this node, which is what makes it the
# "separate layout with only the live services" — there is no detection step and no
# conditional templating. When the house is dark this page is simply still correct,
# because nothing on it depends on the house.
#
# Widget URLs deliberately use the node-local Docker service names on the `proxy` network
# rather than public hostnames. That keeps widget traffic off the auth boundary entirely
# — the cluster's copy has to route its widgets via `-k8s` monitoring hostnames precisely
# because the public route's Authelia 401s them.

- Reading:
    - FreshRSS:
        icon: freshrss.png
        href: https://freshrss.{{ domain }}/
        description: RSS link aggregator
        siteMonitor: http://freshrss:80/
        widget:
            type: freshrss
            url: http://freshrss:80
            username: {{ freshrss_username }}
            password: {{ freshrss_password }}
    - Karakeep:
        icon: karakeep.png
        href: https://karakeep.{{ domain }}/
        description: Bookmark archive
        siteMonitor: http://karakeep:3000/
        widget:
            type: karakeep
            url: http://karakeep:3000
            key: {{ karakeep_homepage_api_key }}

- Status:
    - Uptime Kuma:
        icon: uptime-kuma.png
        href: https://uptime-kuma.{{ domain }}/
        # The watcher outside the house: it is what still answers when daniel-box does not.
        description: Offsite monitoring
        siteMonitor: http://uptime-kuma:3001/
    - Public page:
        icon: si-aboutdotme.png
        href: https://www.{{ domain }}/
        description: littlelink
        siteMonitor: http://littlelink:3000/
